<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of The Hague (1720)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1720</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-quadruple-alliance">War of the Quadruple Alliance</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of The Hague (1720) was signed on 17 February 1720, ending the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-quadruple-alliance">War of the Quadruple Alliance</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-v-of-spain">Philip V of Spain</a> gave up his conquests in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/victor-amadeus-ii">Victor Amadeus II</a> of Savoy exchanged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sicily">Sicily</a> for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sardinia">Sardinia</a> with Emperor Charles VI. The exchange created the Kingdom of Sardinia under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-savoy">House of Savoy</a>, ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turin">Turin</a>, the state that later led the unification of Italy.</p></div>
